{"answer": "{
  "summary": "Root cause: the driver refactor moved the real session body into idma_run_session2() (linux/drivers/misc/idma.c:2254-2607) and left idma_run_session() as a thin wrapper (idma.c:2609-2616) that calls it with cfg=NULL. tests/test_idma_scheduler.py still extracted only 'idma_run_session', so the emitted wrapper body called an undeclared idma_run_session2 (implicit-function-declaration) and every helper that the session body uses (idma_validate, idma_observation_*, idma_snapshot*, idma_verify, idma_batch_window/disable, idma_e3_finish, idma_stream_reseed, idma_gap_*, idma_batch_start_log, riscv_iommu_hpm_acquire/release, mutex_*, idma_put_instance, idma_experiment_lock) became unused (-Wunused-function) under -Werror. That matches the attached regression log exactly.\n\nProposed changes (tests/test_idma_scheduler.py only, 4 small edits):\n1. Add 'idma_run_session2' to FUNCTIONS immediately BEFORE 'idma_run_session'. Ordering matters: the extracted text is emitted in tuple order, so session2 must be defined before the wrapper that calls it, otherwise the implicit-declaration error just moves into the wrapper. This makes the test drive the REAL session2 body through the REAL legacy wrapper with cfg=NULL (no fake session2, no re-implementation of driver logic).\n2. Inject host stand-ins for the five research2 hooks that idma_run_session2 calls but that live in linux/drivers/misc/idma_research.h (idma_research2_preflight, idma_research2_pre_arm, idma_research2_method_freeze, idma_research2_method_abort, idma_research_capture_ext; declared at idma.c:2239-2252). They are injected at the '/* PRODUCTION_FUNCTIONS */' marker so they are defined before the extracted session code. Each returns -EOPNOTSUPP when handed a non-NULL cfg (the void hook is a documented no-op that is only reachable after a non-NULL cfg has already failed the run), so a host run can never be mistaken for validation of the research2 driver path; with cfg==NULL they are never called (all call sites are guarded by `if (cfg)` or by the `cfg ? ... : ...` ternary at idma.c:2551).\n3. Wire that injection into the harness build.\n4. Add a fail-fast check that struct idma_stream still carries touched_tail/reverse. Both fields are already present in the supplied driver (idma.c:127 `size_t size, offset, next_offset, touched_end, touched_tail;` and idma.c:131 `bool batch_configured, batch_started, reverse;`), and the struct is taken from the driver via the '/* PRODUCTION_TYPES */' injection, so nothing has to be added; the check converts silent drift into a clear error instead of a confusing host-compiler failure.\n\nNo production file is touched; the harness file is not edited (only the string injected by the test). No test was executed by me.",
  "edits": [
    {
      "path": "tests/test_idma_scheduler.py",
      "old": "    'idma_run_session', 'idma_run_p4m', 'idma_run_e3_pair', 'idma_run_experiment_mode', 'idma_run_experiment',",
      "new": "    'idma_run_session2', 'idma_run_session', 'idma_run_p4m', 'idma_run_e3_pair', 'idma_run_experiment_mode', 'idma_run_experiment',"
    },
    {
      "path": "tests/test_idma_scheduler.py",
      "old": "CACHE_CASES = ('cache_solo', 'cache_corun', 'cache_real_corruption')\n\n\ndef extract(source, pattern, label):",
      "new": "CACHE_CASES = ('cache_solo', 'cache_corun', 'cache_real_corruption')\n\n# Host stand-ins for the research2 hooks defined in idma_research.h.  The host\n# harness only models legacy cfg==NULL sessions driven through the real\n# idma_run_session() wrapper, so these hooks are unreachable there; they exist\n# so the extracted idma_run_session2() compiles under -Werror.  They refuse a\n# non-NULL cfg instead of pretending to validate the research2 driver path.\nRESEARCH2_HOOKS = '''\\\nstatic int idma_research2_preflight(struct idma_device *d,\n\t\t\t\t    const struct idma_research2_config *cfg)\n{\n\t(void)d;\n\treturn cfg ? -EOPNOTSUPP : 0;\n}\n\nstatic int idma_research2_pre_arm(struct idma_device *d,\n\t\t\t\t  const struct idma_research2_config *cfg)\n{\n\t(void)d;\n\treturn cfg ? -EOPNOTSUPP : 0;\n}\n\nstatic int idma_research2_method_freeze(struct idma_device *d,\n\t\t\t\t\tconst struct idma_research2_config *cfg,\n\t\t\t\t\tint error)\n{\n\t(void)d;\n\t(void)error;\n\treturn cfg ? -EOPNOTSUPP : 0;\n}\n\nstatic void idma_research2_method_abort(struct idma_device *d,\n\t\t\t\t\tconst struct idma_research2_config *cfg,\n\t\t\t\t\tint error)\n{\n\t/* Reached only after a non-NULL cfg has already failed the run. */\n\t(void)d;\n\t(void)cfg;\n\t(void)error;\n}\n\nstatic int idma_research_capture_ext(struct idma_device *d,\n\t\t\t\t     struct idma_research *r,\n\t\t\t\t     const struct idma_research2_config *cfg,\n\t\t\t\t     int error)\n{\n\t(void)d;\n\t(void)r;\n\t(void)error;\n\treturn cfg ? -EOPNOTSUPP : 0;\n}\n'''\n\n\ndef extract(source, pattern, label):"
    },
    {
      "path": "tests/test_idma_scheduler.py",
      "old": "        structures = '\\n'.join(\n            extract(source, rf'^struct {name} \\{{.*?^\\}};', name)\n            for name in ('idma_device', 'idma_stream', 'idma_batch_start',\n                         'idma_observation')\n        )",
      "new": "        structures = '\\n'.join(\n            extract(source, rf'^struct {name} \\{{.*?^\\}};', name)\n            for name in ('idma_device', 'idma_stream', 'idma_batch_start',\n                         'idma_observation')\n        )\n        # idma_run_session2() bookkeeping needs these refactored idma_stream\n        # fields (declared at linux/drivers/misc/idma.c:127,131); fail fast here\n        # instead of letting the host compiler report an unrelated error.\n        for field in ('touched_tail', 'reverse'):\n            if field not in structures:\n                raise RuntimeError(f'production struct idma_stream lacks {field}')"
    },
    {
      "path": "tests/test_idma_scheduler.py",
      "old": "        harness = (ROOT / 'tests/idma_scheduler_harness.c').read_text()\n        harness = harness.replace('/* PRODUCTION_TYPES */', definitions + '\\n' + structures)\n        harness = harness.replace('/* PRODUCTION_FUNCTIONS */', functions)",
      "new": "        harness = (ROOT / 'tests/idma_scheduler_harness.c').read_text()\n        harness = harness.replace('/* PRODUCTION_TYPES */', definitions + '\\n' + structures)\n        # The research2 hooks live in idma_research.h, which the harness does\n        # not compile; inject the legacy-only stand-ins ahead of the extracted\n        # session code so it builds without implicit declarations.\n        harness = harness.replace('/* PRODUCTION_FUNCTIONS */',\n                                  RESEARCH2_HOOKS + '\\n' + functions)"
    }
  ],
  "tests": [
    "Primary acceptance (parent to run; not run here): `python3 -m pytest tests/test_idma_scheduler.py -q` must reach unittest (no setUpClass error) and every subtest of test_production_control_flow, test_small_chunk_device_validation and test_cache_visibility must print 'PASS <case>'. A compile failure prints the whole cc/ld output as the assertion message.",
    "Compile-only reproduction: the setUpClass cc line is copied verbatim in the traceback (tests/test_idma_scheduler.py:97-101); the same command line rerun against the generated scheduler.c is the fastest way to see whether the remaining errors are compile (-Werror) or link (undefined reference).",
    "Expected error-set change: the 21 -Wunused-function errors in the attached log (idma_batch_start_log, idma_verify, idma_snapshot*, idma_observation_*, idma_batch_window/disable, idma_e3_finish, idma_stream_reseed, idma_validate, idma_gap_*, riscv_iommu_hpm_acquire/release, idma_put_instance, mutex_lock_interruptible/mutex_unlock) plus the unused idma_experiment_lock variable must all disappear, because idma_run_session2 now references them; the only remaining failure mode to look for is a duplicate definition or a missing legacy research hook (see risks).",
    "Parent-only sanity greps (cheap, before running): `grep -n 'idma_research2_\\|idma_research_capture_ext' tests/idma_scheduler_harness.c` (must show no definitions of the five hooks, otherwise the injected stand-ins collide in the same TU), `grep -n 'idma_research_begin\\|idma_research_capture\\|idma_research_quiet' tests/idma_scheduler_harness.c` (must show that the pre-refactor research hooks are still provided, since idma_run_session2 keeps calling them at idma.c:2446,2535,2551), and `grep -n 'idma_research2_config' linux/include/uapi/linux/idma.h` (the config struct must be complete, because idma.c:2338 dereferences cfg->reverse).",
    "Explicit scope statement for the record: these host tests exercise only the cfg==NULL legacy path through the real wrapper; a PASS does not validate any research2 (non-NULL cfg) driver behaviour, because the injected hooks deliberately reject a non-NULL cfg."
  ],
  "risks": [
    "tests/idma_scheduler_harness.c was not supplied, so its exact marker layout and existing mocks are inferred. The five stand-ins are injected right before '/* PRODUCTION_FUNCTIONS */' and are `static`; if the harness already defines any of idma_research2_preflight / idma_research2_pre_arm / idma_research2_method_freeze / idma_research2_method_abort / idma_research_capture_ext (or forward-declares them with an incompatible signature), the build will fail with a redefinition/conflict error. The grep check above resolves this before running.",
    "idma_run_session2 also calls idma_research_begin (idma.c:2446), idma_research_quiet (idma.c:2535) and idma_research_capture (idma.c:2552). These were already needed by the pre-refactor idma_run_session, so they are assumed to exist in the harness; if it only declares them without definitions, the fixed build will fail at link time with undefined references and equivalent stand-ins would be needed (out of scope of these four edits, and they must not be added blindly because they may already be defined).",
    "The injected code compiles against `struct idma_research2_config` and `struct idma_research` as provided by the uapi header copied at tests/test_idma_scheduler.py:94 (linux/include/uapi/linux/idma.h -> build/linux/idma.h). If that header does not define idma_research2_config completely, idma.c:2338 (`a->reverse = cfg && cfg->reverse;`) will not compile; that would require a type-import edit that cannot be written blind here.",
    "The stub bodies are intentionally inert for cfg==NULL (unreachable) and return -EOPNOTSUPP for a non-NULL cfg; a future harness that wants real research2 coverage must compile idma_research.h instead of relying on these stand-ins. Do not treat a PASS of this suite as research2 validation.",
    "The touched_tail/reverse addition is a no-op for the supplied driver (both fields already exist at linux/drivers/misc/idma.c:127 and :131); the new guard only raises a clearer error if a future driver revision removes them while the extracted session still uses them.",
    "FUNCTIONS order becomes source-order-critical: if a later edit puts 'idma_run_session' before 'idma_run_session2' in the tuple, the wrapper again calls an undeclared function and -Werror fires.",
    "No execution or compile was performed by this worker; all statements about which errors disappear are derived from the attached log plus the call sites cited in linux/drivers/misc/idma.c, and must be confirmed by the parent's own run."
  ]
